        {
          "type": "graph",
          "say": "Give every ticker exactly one writer thread. A feed hashes the ticker to pick its writer, and sends the event over a single-producer, single-consumer queue, one per feed and writer pair. A ticker always arrives on the same feed, so its events stay in wire order. The writer updates the high and drawdown in plain memory, with no atomics on the math, then publishes the pair with a release store. Readers load it with acquire, and always see a consistent pair.",
