        {
          "type": "code",
          "say": "In code, the slot keeps the writer's high and drawdown as plain doubles, and a sixteen-byte atomic pair for readers. The writer loop pops events in order, updates the two numbers, and publishes with release. A reader finds the slot, and loads the pair with acquire.",
          "props": {
            "title": "The writer and the reader",
            "file": "tracker.cpp",
            "tag": "single writer",
            "lang": "cpp",
            "size": 21,
            "width": 1180,
            "code": "struct alignas(64) TickerSlot {\n    double w_high = -INFINITY, w_max_dd = 0;     // writer-only: plain memory\n    std::atomic<PairView> published;            // (high, max_dd) for readers\n};\n\n// One writer thread owns this queue, and every ticker hashed to it.\nvoid WriterLoop(SPSCQueue<Event>& q) {\n    Event e;\n    while (q.WaitAndPop(e)) {\n        auto* s = e.slot;\n        if (e.price > s->w_high) s->w_high = e.price;\n        double dd = s->w_high - e.price;\n        if (dd > s->w_max_dd) s->w_max_dd = dd;\n        s->published.store({s->w_high, s->w_max_dd},\n                           std::memory_order_release);\n    }\n}\n\nstd::optional<double> GetMaxDrawdown(const std::string& ticker) const {\n    auto* s = registry_.Find(ticker);\n    if (!s) return std::nullopt;\n    return s->published.load(std::memory_order_acquire).max_dd;\n}",
            "highlights": [
